      "text": "blessed are they who seek to bring forth Zion, 1 Ne. 13:37. land is consecrated unto him whom the Lord shall bring, 2 Ne. 1:7. if ye are brought up in way ye should go, ye will not depart from it, 2 Ne. 4:5 (Prov. 22:6). because men ask not, they are not brought into light, 2 Ne. 32:4. perhaps thou shalt say, The man has brought upon himself his misery, Mosiah 4:17. they shall see eye to eye when the Lord shall bring again Zion, Mosiah 12:22 (15:29; 3 Ne. 16:18). God will not suffer believers to be destroyed until they bring it upon themselves by transgressions, Alma 46:18. faith and repentance bring change of heart, Hel. 15:7. other sheep I have, them also I must bring, 3 Ne. 15:17, 21 (John 10:16).",
